    "risk_summary": "Geoopt0 prints BFGS failure, but geoopt1 prints later positive convergence/no failure and low force. Coarse source stress is near zero; fine stress is anisotropic (−.567,−.567,+.861 GPa). This is finite basin support, not proof of a thermodynamic ambient ground state.",
    "ambient_scope": "The exact source neutral zero-applied-pressure model has positive Γ optical compression intervals and no negative retained sampled path value for target and selected control. Coarse/fine force and full stress, relaxation warnings and every q record are retained. These finite observations do not prove full-BZ or thermodynamic hull stability.",
    "route_response": "Hf→Ti on the matched ordered cation role raises weighted ωlog by 12.60–13.39% while λ drops .0171–.0229 at every token. Source fixed μ*=.1 McMillan/AD/Eli outputs all improve; separate-header proxy crosses below one at μ*=.2, so the positive claim is explicitly source-μ-limited.",
    "next_action": "Discriminate the ordered SG166 phase from the known rocksalt nanophase, and read saved α²F weights plus fine-strain response. A realistic μ or strain correction can reverse the net benefit; do not extrapolate the source μ=.1 result to high physical probability.",
