      "pairing_relevance": "Separate source Eli gain 0.88 K is retained with source McMillan/AD. Actual source-header descriptor reproduces the first McMillan column to printed precision. Header-to-ten-σ and Eli-to-σ association remains null, and ωlog is α²F weighted rather than an assertion that all bare modes harden.",
      "ambient_feasibility": "The exact source neutral zero-applied-pressure model has positive Γ optical compression intervals and no negative retained sampled path value for target and selected control. Coarse/fine force and full stress, relaxation warnings and every q record are retained. These finite observations do not prove full-BZ or thermodynamic hull stability.",
      "competition_and_coherence": "Geoopt0 prints BFGS failure, but geoopt1 prints later positive convergence/no failure and low force. Coarse source stress is near zero; fine stress is anisotropic (−.567,−.567,+.861 GPa). This is finite basin support, not proof of a thermodynamic ambient ground state.",
